SUMMARY:SR Laws at Cafe Frida
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passion for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in your head while still delivering ideas completely unique. He draws inspiration from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lucinda Williams\, Steve Earle\, Neil Finn\, Patty Griffin\, R E.M. and Ron Sexsmith\, among others. Their music has played a significant role in shaping his artistic journey. \nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he developed a unique connection to music early on. His father worked as a trash collector\, and he would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 records. Each find felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were covered in dirt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of discovering new sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop the needle and immerse himself in the music.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/sr-laws-at-cafe-frida-7/
LOCATION:Cafe Frida Gallery\, 300 South A Street #4\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Music
GEO:38.43412;-122.71481
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Cafe Frida Gallery 300 South A Street #4 Santa Rosa CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=300 South A Street #4:geo:-122.71481,38.43412
END:VEVENT
